{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"73651a459f29dd7450c6c7cc39df246c43793a49"},"timestamp":1536875077,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMTE2MzIyMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2828#issuecomment-421163221"},"message":"[GitMate.io](https://gitmate.io) thinks possibly related issues are https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2824 ([question] DataLad Questions Set 1: Relationship to Git Annex), https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1193 (datalad mv), https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2693 (datalad aliases), https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2825 ([question] levels of a dataset), and https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/227 (datalad get  barfes).","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1536891577,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE4NDUwNjU1MzQ="},"added":["question"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1536891964,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMTIxMDY3MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2828#issuecomment-421210670"},"message":"- multiple extractors -- as many as you like. See e.g. http://datasets.datalad.org/openfmri/ds000001/.datalad/config where for BIDS datasets we typically enable `nifti1`, `xmp`, and `bids` extractors.\n- validation -- your extractor can do whatever **you** like it to do ;)  in our case majority of extractors, which do not have strong assumptions/idea about what to expect would just skip a file if extraction fails. But `bids` extractor might just blow the entire extraction if something is not entirely kosher, so treat it as a feature/validation ;-)\n\nFeel welcome to close the issue whenever answer satisfies ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1536905344,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMTI0MTY3MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2828#issuecomment-421241671"},"message":"I would be curious to learn about what kind of \"custom logic\" would be desirable, and how that would fit into our metadata model.\n\nThat being said: DataLad will not try to *understand* your metadata, it is more like a transport layer for metadata -- garbage in, garbage out  ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"3286e9a6aeeb25e1bf3fcf613be9da3d3270e55d"},"timestamp":1536930588,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMTM1MzE5OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2828#issuecomment-421353199"},"message":"Ok cool - yes my understanding (and I agree with this!) is that validation is out of scope of datalad, and actually the bids validator is a perfect example of how validation should be. It does make sense that some custom validator might be integrated into datalad via a custom extractor OR just run on the dataset before interacting with datalad, period. BIDS validator is a good example for data in a browser (or on the filesystem) as is something like the [Google Schema Validator](https://developers.google.com/search/docs/guides/prototype) for the same metadata embedded in web pages. \n\nI think what we we would is to be able to:\n - read in a metadata description file (this is meta.json correct?)\n - parse over the root and then identify where data is missing, incorrectly formatted, or other.\n\nTwo questions: Do you think this could be provided generally for (a large number or many) schemas, and do you think the maximum amount of integration with datalad would be a plugin sort of deal? I think it would be ideal to be able to run it external to datalad or any other tool, e.g. let's say we have a folder at `root` with a bunch of subfolders, each with a \"meta.json\" file to describe content within:\n\n```bash\n./validate \u003croot\u003e\n```\nShould validate that. This setup would imply that:\n -  a single folder with a `meta.json` has the meta.json describing all content within\n -  for an exception we provided a custom `meta-\u003cfilename\u003e-` file to describe `\u003cfile\u003e`\n - or we have a filter within a specific `meta.json` to do the same\n\nThoughts?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1537165663,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMTkwMTY0OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2828#issuecomment-421901648"},"message":"Nothing but one important thing would prevent a validation mechanism to be bolted on. That one thing is a machine-readable schema to base validation on. I am not talking about the technology, but real implementations for real standard. The BIDS validator would require its software stack to become a dependency (if that would be a feasible model). That quickly becomes infeasible when scaled up to 10-15 standards.\n\nNote that `meta.json` is a outdated thing that @yarikoptic keeps around in the central dataset, please ignore it.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"3286e9a6aeeb25e1bf3fcf613be9da3d3270e55d"},"timestamp":1537203120,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMjA4OTk1Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2828#issuecomment-422089957"},"message":"yeah @yarikoptic told me! Thanks for the additional tidbits @mih. I've been quiet this weekend working on this --\u003e https://github.com/BioSchemas/map2model/pull/35\nin case you have comment! It's a template to produce a specification for bioschema, and the implementation I added **does** have validation, albeit for the specification files and not data they will describe. This would need to be done first before I create a dataset that would be managed by datalad and described by a bioschema.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1570266485,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUzODYzMjE5OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2828#issuecomment-538632198"},"message":"Closing \"question\"-type issue with a response, and no further activity.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1570266485,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjY4OTE4NTk3OA=="},"status":2}]}